Patch: fix diver scanner crash on empty discrete-parameter vector
==================================================================

Applies to the gambit_light checkout ($GAMBIT_LIGHT_DIR), file:
    ScannerBit/src/scanners/diver_1.3.0/diver.cpp

WHY
---
With `use_scanner: diver` and no discrete parameters (nDiscrete == 0, the
default), the plugin passes `&discrete[0]` of an empty `std::vector<int>` to
cdiver(). That is undefined behaviour. In a gambit_light built with
Homebrew gcc-15, whose libstdc++ has bounds-checking active (BUILD_TYPE: None,
empty CXX_FLAGS, no -DNDEBUG), `operator[]` aborts:

    .../c++/15/bits/stl_vector.h:1263: ... Assertion '__n < this->size()' failed.

It is independent of `initial_guesses` — it fires on any diver run with no
discrete params. (The `random` scanner never hits this code path, which is why
earlier smoke runs were fine.)

FIX (one line): use `.data()` instead of `&v[0]`. `.data()` on an empty vector
returns a valid pointer and never trips the bounds assertion; cdiver gets
nDiscrete=0 and does not dereference it.

--- a/ScannerBit/src/scanners/diver_1.3.0/diver.cpp
+++ b/ScannerBit/src/scanners/diver_1.3.0/diver.cpp
@@ cdiver call (~line 204-208)
     cdiver(&objective, nPar, &lowerbounds[0], &upperbounds[0], &path[0], nDerived, &bestFitParams[0],
-           bestFitDerived, nDiscrete, &discrete[0], partitionDiscrete, maxgen, NP, nF, &Fvec[0], Cr,
+           bestFitDerived, nDiscrete, discrete.data(), partitionDiscrete, maxgen, NP, nF, &Fvec[0], Cr,
            lambda, current, expon, bndry, jDE, lambdajDE, convthresh, convsteps, removeDuplicates,
            savecount, resume, disableIO, outputRaw, outputSam, init_pop_strategy, nGuesses, &initial_guesses[0],
            discard_unfit_points, max_ini_attempts, max_acceptable_value, seed, context, verbose);

REAPPLY / REBUILD
-----------------
This edit lives outside this repo (in the gambit checkout) and is lost if gambit
is re-pulled or reinstalled. To reapply by hand, make the one-character-ish edit
above, then rebuild ONLY the plugin (gambit dlopens it at runtime; gambit itself
is not relinked):

    cd $GAMBIT_LIGHT_DIR/build && make scanner_diver_1.3.0
    # relinks ScannerBit/lib/libscanner_diver_1.3.0.so

VERIFIED
--------
After the fix, `use_scanner: diver` runs to EXIT=0 / "GAMBIT has finished
successfully!", seeds the 3 `initial_guesses` points, and writes
Oh2 = 0.120038 / 0.119815 / 0.120087 (the seeded relic-ridge points) as the
first three samples.
